    "problem_statement": "A thread needs a way to check whether it has permission to access a given kernel object before attempting an operation on it, so it can fail gracefully instead of faulting. The check should return 0 when the object is valid and the calling thread has access, -EPERM when the object is valid but the calling thread has no access, and -EBADF when the supplied address is not a valid kernel object. The check must also report 0 for the calling thread's own thread object, since a thread always has access to itself.",
